# 8. Duplicate File Detection

Duplicate detection must be based on durable business and technical identifiers.

Consider:

* File checksum
* File name
* File creation/arrival date
* Vendor/source
* NACHA file identification
* Business date
* Other vendor-specific identifiers

A file with identical content must not be processed twice.

Duplicate detection must remain effective after application restart or database failover.

